  "description": "Harness item T23 (fixed; found in the formats family's sample after the P44 fix, seed 23507, 5000 cases): the oracle's interval_is_wall() (research/php-oracle/lib.php) probed an interval by adding and subtracting it around the end of DST in New York, and missed the wall-clock mode of a `new DateInterval()` when the interval's date part or a long time part kept that arithmetic from crossing the offset change. The typed tree then lacked `\"wall\": true`, twig-fuzz rebuilt the interval in civil mode, and twig-rs took its time part in civil time: formats-23507-841, `{{ date(v0, 'Europe/Dublin').sub(v2)|date(v1, false) }}` with `P9MT62825H6M7S`, came out one hour later than in PHP. The probe now takes a clone of the interval (which keeps the mode) with its date part dropped and one second as its time part. These vectors were recorded with that probe: the wall-clock intervals carry `\"wall\": true` (with the old probe twig-rs got each of them one hour wrong), the controls are civil intervals and an interval without a time part, which carry no mark. Every vector must stay identical. Recorded with \"isolation\": \"process\".",
